From 04ccf5e15b9159ff5959f89a0ec5af65e5a9831f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahtyor <pepsykolya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:45:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] FreeForgeMiner 1.2.3: faster fused kernel, persistent
 eco kernel (cfg 13)

Strength-reduced main loop (per-thread offsets once, ldmatrix k-steps by XOR, cp.async shared
offsets as immediates, column-outer MMA order); epilogue in the K domain (limb weights
K 2^(8j) mod p with K^3 = R^5: one Montgomery reduction and two products give the canonical
cube; signed mad.wide; per-tile column/row term tables; transposed limb stores through shared
memory). Persistent 128x256 BK128 kernel (cfg 13) with per-layer atomic tile tickets, next-tile
prefetch during the epilogue and alternating K direction. Defaults: RTX 30 (small L2) speed =
cfg 0, eco = cfg 13; RTX 40/50 (large L2) cfg 13 in both modes. Output bit-identical to the
reference on sm_86 and sm_89.
RTX 3070 1560 MHz +175: cfg0 20.69 FW/s @178 W, cfg13 20.10 @155 W (1.2.2: 19.92 @184, 18.65 @159).
RTX 4070 Ti 2100 MHz +150 190 W: cfg13 34.80 FW/s @178 W (1.2.2 default 30.62 @190 W).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
